From 92c0a8cf14486dae1ce46d79a2649fb0bae5ff2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gargrohin <29701609+gargrohin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:02:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cosmos3_Nano: eval adapter for a cosmos-framework RoboTwin
 action policy

Serves a Cosmos3-Nano policy post-trained with cosmos-framework's
action_policy_robotwin_nano recipe (aloha_agilex, 14-D absolute joint
positions) through the XPolicyLab policy server. Per query the adapter
rebuilds the training sample for the current moment, with the settings read
from the run's config.yaml: head and wrist cameras composed as in training,
the normalized state as the conditioning action row, the JSON prompt (idle
frames 0), the training transform. It returns the 16 generated actions,
denormalized, in the GR00T_N17 per-step dict format.

Checkpoints are DCP iterations of a cosmos-framework run dir, resolved through
the shared checkpoint resolver (run_dir key) and loaded with OmniInference
(EMA weights by default); a checkpoint newer than latest_checkpoint.txt is
refused. Sampling defaults follow NVIDIA's LIBERO policy server (30 UniPC
steps, guidance 1.0, shift 5.0). Two warm-up generations run before the port
opens so compilation cannot time out the client's first request.

Eval-only and local: no install/process_data/train/eval scripts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
